{
 "about": "Where the order of evaluation reaches. In each case one child fails the decision when it is evaluated: its only rule is ALLOW with the condition subject.parityR22Failing == 'v', and that GENERAL PIP answers 500. Its sibling permits unconditionally. The pair is two ALLOW rules of one policy, two policies of one set, two nested sets of one set, or two sets at the top, under DENY_UNLESS_PERMIT and PERMIT_OVERRIDES, where a permit is final. Each case has a check and a filter request, both classed by the failing PIP's route, so a golden says whether the failing child was evaluated. Record on several stands. A request that shows one class on every stand is an answer too: a filter that evaluates every policy and set reads the PIP whatever the order.",
